data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01YWRNWLZV2ifCoMpS92S6bt","output":" 1  ---\n 2  name: action-recommendation\n 3  description: >-\n 4    Generate concrete, prioritized action recommendations from financial insights.\n 5    ALWAYS included as the final step of every data analysis and report output.\n 6    Combines wiki knowledge (campaigns, products, pricing) with LLM banking\n 7    expertise to produce specific next-step actions grounded in data evidence.\n 8    Actions MUST pass the Relevance Test — only include actions that directly\n 9    move the underperforming metric for the exact segment/product being analyzed.\n10  ---\n11  \n12  ## Core Principle: Direct Causality\n13  \n14  Every action must have a **direct causal path** to the metric gap identified. \"Direct\" = the action moves the metric within 1 logical step, no intermediary assumptions.\n15  \n16  Test: if the CEO asks \"how does this action fix the problem we just discussed?\", the answer must be immediate and obvious — not \"if X then Y then Z\".\n17  \n18  ## Workflow\n19  \n20  1. **Identify gaps** — which metrics underperform, by how much, which segments drag\n21  2. **Define scope boundary** — lock segment, product, geography, time period. Actions MUST stay within this boundary.\n22  3. **Relevance Test** (MANDATORY) — `read_file` → `references/relevance-test.md`. Every candidate action passes 3 gates.\n23  4. **Wiki lookup** — grep the wiki for the campaigns, products and pricing that address the gap. The search always happens; what is conditional is what you keep from it — content aimed at a different segment stays out (Rule 8).\n24  5. **Synthesize** — filtered context + banking expertise → 3–5 concrete actions\n25  6. **Evaluate & Score** — `read_file` → `references/evaluation-criteria.md`. Score 5 dimensions, apply elimination rules.\n26  7. **Market enrichment** — `read_file` → `skills/market-intelligence/SKILL.md`, then follow it: map each action's metric gap → topic in `query-catalog.md`, call `web_search`, inject `market_signal` into the Why field. One thing skips this step: `web_search` returning a status other than `ok`. Then keep the actions as they are and say nothing about it.\n27  8. **Format** — per template below\n28  \n29  ## References (read on demand)\n30  \n31  | File | When to read | Content |\n32  | --- | --- | --- |\n33  | `references/relevance-test.md` | Step 3: before including any action | 3 Gates, Causal Chain, Wiki decision tree |\n34  | `references/evaluation-criteria.md` | Step 6: after generating candidates | 5-dimension rubric, scoring guide, priority formula |\n35  | `references/anti-patterns.md` | When unsure if action belongs | 4 anti-patterns with wrong/right examples, scope-locked pattern |\n36  | `skills/market-intelligence/SKILL.md` | Action generation: market signal enrichment | When/how to call web_search, interpret results, inject signals |\n37  | `skills/market-intelligence/query-catalog.md` | Action generation: query selection | Topic-to-query mapping, domains, recency windows |\n38  \n39  ## Action Format\n40  \n41  ```\n42  **🔴/🟡/🟢 [Priority] Action Title**\n43  - Why: Data evidence (exact metric/gap + root cause)\n44    📡 Market Signal: <key_signal from web_search> (optional, only when available)\n45  - Action: Specific steps (1-3 concrete actions)\n46  - Impact: Quantified metric improvement (direct path only)\n47  - Owner: Team/role responsible\n48  ```\n49  \n50  ## Priority Levels\n51  \n52  - 🔴 **High** — Impact >30% gap, feasible now, 1-step causal chain within same segment\n53  - 🟡 **Medium** — 10-30% gap closure, needs coordination, still direct\n54  - 🟢 **Long-term** — <10% or cross-functional dependency (rare — most should be 🔴/🟡)\n55  \n56  **Hard rule:** Directness=1 (multi-step or different scope) → can NEVER be 🔴.\n57  \n58  ## Rules\n59  \n60  1. **Relevance Test first** — every action passes 3 gates before formatting\n61  2. **Scope-locked** — actions stay within the segment/product/geography being analyzed\n62  3. **Ground in data** — every action cites the specific metric/gap from the analysis\n63  4. **Wiki scope-locked** — search it every time; reference only the content matching the scope boundary\n64  5. **Be concrete** — BAD: \"Increase CASA\". GOOD: \"CASA payroll for HH customers earning ≥30M, target +20K B in Q3\"\n65  6. **Max 5 actions** — highest-leverage, scope-matched, ordered by priority\n66  7. **Match user language** — Vietnamese query → Vietnamese actions; English query → English actions\n67  8. **No borrowed campaigns** — campaign targets different segment → do NOT include, even \"adapted\"\n68  9. **Cross-segment insights** → separate \"Additional Notes\" section (NOT in action list)\n69  \n70  ## HTML Report Integration\n71  \n72  Placement: `SECTIONS → ... → ACTIONS → FOOTER`\n73  \n74  Uses: priority badges (🔴/🟡/🟢) · card layout (Why/Action/Impact/Owner) · collapsible details\n75  ","duration_ms":0}}

